=begin
  dreavening_weapon.lic

  During a Dreavening, keeps your weapon in your right (main) hand so it gets blessed.

  Why: Dreaven's blessing goes to the weapon in your main hand ("Your weapon has been
  blessed. If you have another weapon you want blessed be sure to move it to your main
  hand now."). The ;dreavening script's eat_that_bread routine does `stow right` to free
  the hand for the manna bread / tart, `get`s the food and `gob`s it -- and never puts the
  weapon back (10/25: `[dreavening]>stow right` at 15:09:14 stowed the runestaff, then
  `get tart` / `gob my tart`). So after eating, your hands are empty when the blessing
  comes round.

  What it does: it's on in Dreaven's room and off everywhere else. The moment Dreaven is
  in the room with you, that room counts as the Dreavening room; it stays on there (even
  while he crawls under the table to hide and drops out of the room list) until you're in
  any other room. While it's on, if your right hand has been empty for 3 seconds in a row
  -- long enough that ;dreavening has finished eating, since it is holding food the whole
  time it's eating -- it does `ready weapon`. If the weapon is in your LEFT hand and the
  right is empty, it does `swap`. Anywhere else it does nothing at all, so it won't
  interfere with scrolls, wands, instruments or anything else that has your hands.

  History: 10/25 and 10/27 versions tried to tell when a Dreavening was on from what
  Dreaven said, and kept readying the weapon after it ended -- on 10/27 four times at the
  lockers, 12 rooms away. His [Dreavening]-GSIV: lines (FINISHED included) are LNet chat
  that never reaches a script, and the "is Dreaven here?" check broke when you were alone.
  Being in his room is the whole test now. GameObj.pcs is nil, not [], when nobody else is
  in the room, hence the Array().

  Usage:
    ;dreavening_weapon            start it (stays running; ;kill dreavening_weapon stops it)
    ;autostart add --global dreavening_weapon     to start it with every character, like
                                                  ;dreavening itself

  It never touches dreavening.lic. Tunables (below) are methods, so an edit applies the
  next time the script starts.
=end

# seconds the right hand must stay empty before the weapon comes back out
def hold_secs; 3; end

def dreaven_here?
  Array(GameObj.pcs).any? { |pc| pc.noun == "Dreaven" }
end

echo "dreavening_weapon: will keep your weapon in your main hand while you're in Dreaven's room."

# XMLData.room_count goes up every time you move, so it names "this visit to this room"
dreaven_room = nil
empty_since = nil
loop do
  sleep 1

  dreaven_room = XMLData.room_count if dreaven_here?
  if dreaven_room != XMLData.room_count || dead?
    empty_since = nil
    next
  end

  if checkright
    empty_since = nil
    next
  end

  empty_since ||= Time.now.to_f
  next if Time.now.to_f - empty_since < hold_secs

  waitrt?
  if checkleft && GameObj.left_hand.type.to_s =~ /weapon/
    echo "dreavening_weapon: weapon is in your left hand -- swapping it to the main hand."
    fput "swap"
  else
    echo "dreavening_weapon: right hand is empty in Dreaven's room -- readying your weapon."
    fput "ready weapon"
  end
  empty_since = nil
  sleep 5 # give it time to land before looking again
end
